course: dictionary
lesson: 15471
title: Stoutly: firm and strong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stoutly means bravely and firmly, without giving in. When someone does something stoutly, they keep going or keep saying no, even when it is hard. Look for clue words around it, such as refused, defended or denied. «The little boat stoutly held its place against the wind.» The boat did not move, even in strong wind, so stoutly means firmly and without giving way.
explain: Stoutly can also describe things. A stoutly built door or boot is made strong and thick, so it is hard to break. «The door was stoutly built from solid oak.» Ask yourself: what would a strong, solid door be like? It would be thick and hard to break, which is the meaning here.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «She stoutly refused to change her answer» becomes «She firmly refused to change her answer», which still makes sense. If your meaning fits, you are probably right.
fact: Stoutly means bravely, firmly and strongly, without giving in.
fact: «Stoutly» can describe how someone acts: «The guard stoutly defended the gate.»
fact: «Stoutly built» means made strong and thick: «a stoutly built boat».
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the animals defend their home stoutly against danger.
fact: Clue words for stoutly include refused, defended, denied and held firm.
exercise: «The little dog stoutly refused to let go of the rope.» What does stoutly mean? | Sadly, with tears | Quietly and sleepily | Very quickly, like a race | *Firmly and bravely, without giving in
exercise: «The door was stoutly built from solid oak.» What does stoutly built mean? | *Made strong and thick | Made very small | Painted in bright colours | Built in a hurry and broken
exercise: Ben says stoutly means loudly. Is he right? | Only when someone is shouting | *No, it means bravely and firmly, without giving in | Yes, it always means loud | It means slowly and quietly
test: «The soldiers stoutly guarded the gate all night.» What does stoutly mean here? | *Bravely and firmly, without giving up | Sleepily and slowly | Noisily, with lots of shouting | Happily, while singing
test: Which word means firmly and bravely, without giving in? | *stoutly | sleepily | stolen | softly
exam: Which sentence uses stoutly correctly? | The bell stoutly rang at noon. | The rain stoutly fell on the hill. | *He stoutly stood his ground, though the wind pushed hard against him. | She stoutly ate her crisps in the bath.
